# ARIA Sentinel — environment reference. Copy to .env.local ONLY for development; a customer install needs none of
# this. .env.local is read by the main process at launch; .env.example ships in the package as documentation.

# ---- Runtime (developer overrides; leave UNSET on a customer machine) --------------------------------------------
# Live fixes are a consent-gated SETTING the person turns on in Setup / Settings (audit M1). This override is for
# developers only: 1 forces live fixes ON, 0 forces them OFF (the toggle becomes inert), unset = the stored consent.
#ARIA_SENTINEL_ALLOW_SYSTEM_FIXES=
# Every fix previews only (RUN 13 global dry-run) — a second developer safety, unset in production.
#ARIA_SENTINEL_DRY_RUN=

# ServiceNow incident bridge (the customer's OWN instance only). Leave blank for local dry-run.
# When all three are set, ARIA raises routed incidents and lists the user's tickets.
SN_INSTANCE_URL=
SN_USER=
SN_PASS=

# Per-customer scoping is set by MDM, not env: drop a customer.json into
#   %USERPROFILE%\.aria-sentinel\customer.json   ->  { "customerId": "...", "disabled": false }
# Setting "disabled": true puts THIS install into detect-only (per-customer kill switch).
# An IT lead can also drop %USERPROFILE%\.aria-sentinel\policy.json (disable recipes, business hours) — see
# docs/distribution/INTUNE_MSI_SILENT_INSTALL.md.

# ---- Build machine only (never on a customer PC; never commit real values) ---------------------------------------
# Windows code signing — ONE of the two blocks, set in %USERPROFILE%\.aria-sentinel-signing.bat (loaded by
# build-installer.bat / ota-build.bat) rather than here. docs/SIGNING.md explains both.
#   Azure Trusted Signing (≈ US$9.99/month Basic; identity validation first):
#     AZURE_SIGNING_ENDPOINT=https://eus.codesigning.azure.net   (your region's endpoint)
#     AZURE_SIGNING_ACCOUNT=<Trusted Signing account name>
#     AZURE_SIGNING_PROFILE=<certificate profile name>
#     AZURE_SIGNING_PUBLISHER=CN=Integrated IT Support Inc.      (optional; the subject on the profile)
#     AZURE_TENANT_ID= / AZURE_CLIENT_ID= / AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=  (a service principal, or `az login` instead)
#   OV/EV certificate file (.pfx / .p12):
#     CSC_LINK=C:\path\to\certificate.pfx        (path, https URL, or base64 of the file)
#     CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=<pfx password>
# Without either block the SAME build command produces ARIA-Sentinel-<v>-unsigned.exe and says so.
#
# Publishing (scripts/publish-github-release.mjs, scripts/publish-manifest.mjs, ota-build.bat):
#   GITHUB_TOKEN=            repo scope on the releases repo (or GITHUB_TOKEN_FILE=<path to a file holding it>)
#   GITHUB_RELEASE_REPO=     owner/repo of a PUBLIC releases-only repo (recommended once the source repo goes private)
#   SENTINEL_ADMIN_TOKEN=    the Netlify admin token the manifest publish endpoint checks (X-Admin-Token)
#   SENTINEL_BINARY_URL=     https URL you host the installer at yourself (skips the GitHub Release)
#   SENTINEL_MANDATORY=1     flag the published version as a mandatory update
#   IISUPP_BASE=             defaults to https://iisupp.net
